-- title:
--   Igusa-chart dichotomy transported from the Gauss line, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$ (hypothesis `hq2`), $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$ (hypothesis `hqM'`), and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of [`ValuationSubring.LiesOverPrime`](def/FLTPrelim_Ramification.html#L16), i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (hypothesis `hA`).
--
--   The two function fields involved are `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$, and `fieldBar q M'`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of the curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ for $H=$ `levelH q M'` (the kernel of a unit-group reduction map out of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$); `hle` is the inclusion of the former in the latter. Finally `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` is the level-$M'$ function field over the residue field of $A$, generated by the reductions of the $q$-expansions of $j$ and of $j(q^{M'})$.
--
--   The data are as follows.
--
--   *Supersingular places.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` (a place being a valuation subring containing the constants, not equal to the whole field, with principal ideals), and `hW` says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of places $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places, and whose value at the geometric $j$-generator lies in the supersingular set `ssJSet q`.
--
--   *Constant reduction.* $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto the characteristic-$q$ field with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of elements with nonzero residue, the contraction of `R₀.integers` to the constants being $A$, and the residues of constants being the residues in $A$. The hypothesis `hR₀` states the compatibility of $R_0$ with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   *Uniformiser and root of unity.* $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$ (hypotheses `hπ`, `hπP`); $\zeta$ is an element of `Idx q`, the set of primitive $q$-th roots of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$.
--
--   *The two families of valuation rings of `fieldBar q M'`.* `OIg` is indexed by [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) $=\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and `OSS` by $W$. Four hypotheses govern `OIg`: `hIg_inf` describes the ring at the Gauss line `lineInfty q` $=[1:0]$, namely $f\in$ `OIg (lineInfty q)` if and only if there are Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero coefficientwise reduction and $f\cdot\bar y=\bar x$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$, where bars denote coefficientwise inclusion of $A$; `hIg` says each $\ell$ is $\,$`redQ q γ • lineInfty q` for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with `OIg ℓ` the contraction of `OIg (lineInfty q)` along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` says `OIg` is injective; `hIg_perm` says that for every $\zeta'$ and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ contraction along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family `OIg`. Four hypotheses govern `OSS`: `hSS_A` says the contraction of each `OSS s` to the constants is $A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s\in W$ and $f\in$ `R₀.integers` which is regular at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which $\hat\jmath$ (the image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of $j$) is regular, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s`, and for every $a\in A$ whose residue equals the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of the image of $f$ and the image of $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`; `hSS_fix` says each `OSS s` is stable under contraction along every `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` says each `OSS s` contains an element $t$ such that $t-a$ is a unit of `OSS s` for every $a\in A$.
--
--   *Descent data.* $K_0$ is a subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over which $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is algebraic and which contains $\pi$; $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation domain, $\iota:A_0\to A$ an injective local ring homomorphism whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is exactly $A\cap K_0$ (hypothesis `hιK₀`), with residue map of $A$ composed with $\iota$ surjective (`hres`); $\varpi_0$ generates the maximal ideal of $A_0$ (`hϖ₀`) and its image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $\pi$ (`hϖ₀π`).
--
--   *The descended field.* $F_0$ is a subfield of `fieldBar q M'` characterised by `hF₀`: $f\in F_0$ precisely when all Laurent coefficients of $f$ lie in $K_0$. By `hjF₀` the element $\hat\jmath$, the image in `fieldBar q M'` of the base-changed $q$-expansion of $j$, lies in $F_0$; below $\hat\jmath$ also denotes the corresponding element of $F_0$. An $A_0$-algebra structure on $F_0$ is given, with `hj₀` asserting that its structure map sends $a$ to the image of $\iota(a)$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   *The hypothesis `hinf`.* The dichotomy stated below is assumed for the single line `lineInfty q`: for every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ all of whose elements map into `OIg (lineInfty q)` and such that some element of $F_0$ mapping into `OIg (lineInfty q)` is not in $V$, either there exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$ satisfying the thirteen clauses listed in the conclusion with `lineInfty q` in place of $\ell$ — the clause on $\hat\jmath$ being there in the stronger form $\hat\jmath\in B$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1}\in B$ — or there is $s\in W$ such that every $g\in F_0$ integral over $A_0[\hat\jmath\,]$ whose image lies in the maximal ideal of `OSS s` is a non-unit of $V$.
--
--   The conclusion is the same dichotomy for every line. For every $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb Z/q)$ and every valuation subring $V$ of $F_0$ such that every $f\in V$ has image in `OIg ℓ`, and such that some $f\in F_0$ with image in `OIg ℓ` does not lie in $V$, at least one of the following two alternatives holds.
--
--   First alternative: there exist an $A_0$-subalgebra $B$ of $F_0$ and a maximal ideal $\mathfrak m$ of $B$ such that, writing $\varpi_0B$ for the ideal of $B$ generated by the image of the maximal ideal of $A_0$:
--   (i) $B$ is a finitely generated $A_0$-algebra;
--   (ii) every $x\in F_0$ integral over $B$ lies in $B$;
--   (iii) every $x\in F_0$ is of the form $b/c$ with $b,c\in B$, $c\neq0$;
--   (iv) every non-maximal prime of $B$ containing $\varpi_0B$ is a minimal prime of $\varpi_0B$;
--   (v) for every nonzero prime $\mathfrak p$ of $B$ not containing $\varpi_0B$ there is a valuation subring $V_1$ of $F_0$ whose elements are exactly the quotients $b/c$ with $b,c\in B$ and $c\notin\mathfrak p$;
--   (vi) if all of $B$ maps into `OIg ℓ'` for a line $\ell'$, then $\ell'=\ell$;
--   (vii) for no $s\in W$ does all of $B$ map into `OSS s`;
--   (viii) there is a prime $\mathfrak q$ of $B$ such that, for $x\in F_0$, the image of $x$ lies in `OIg ℓ` if and only if $x=b/c$ with $b,c\in B$, $c\notin\mathfrak q$;
--   (ix) for every minimal prime $\mathfrak q$ of $\varpi_0B$ the same description holds: the image of $x\in F_0$ lies in `OIg ℓ` if and only if $x=b/c$ with $b,c\in B$, $c\notin\mathfrak q$;
--   (x) $B\subseteq V$;
--   (xi) for $b\in B$, $b\in\mathfrak m$ if and only if $b$ is a non-unit of $V$;
--   (xii) either $\hat\jmath$ or $\hat\jmath^{-1}$ is of the form $b/c$ with $b,c\in B$ and $c\notin\mathfrak m$ (a weaker clause than the corresponding one in `hinf`, where membership in $B$ itself is required);
--   (xiii) the structure map $A_0\to$ `Localization.AtPrime 𝔪` is formally smooth.
--
--   Second alternative: there is $s\in W$ such that every $g\in F_0$ which is integral over the $A_0$-subalgebra of $F_0$ generated by $\hat\jmath$ and whose image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `OSS s` and in the maximal ideal of `OSS s`, is a non-unit of $V$.
--
--   This is the level-transport step on the Igusa leg of the construction of a semistable covering of the full-level modular curve at $q=2$: the chart dichotomy, known for the Gauss branch $\ell=\infty$, is propagated to all branches $\ell\in\mathbb P^1(\mathbb F_q)$ using that $\Gamma_0(M')$ acts transitively on the lines through the automorphisms `levelAutBar`, permuting the Igusa rings and fixing each supersingular ring. It feeds the corresponding statement phrased in terms of the Igusa ring itself.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_subalgebra_centred_formallySmooth_or_exists_forall_mem_nonunits_of_forall_gaussBranch_descent_local_of_eq_two.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCovering
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SupersingularNodePlaces
